e dread, and practical effects horror of Carpenter's film contributed significantly to the terrifying aspects of the Upside Down and the Demogorgon in 'Stranger Things'."},{"source":"work_aw35","target":"work_aw321","type":"work_work","relation_type":"influenced","relation_note":"The season's subplot involving a secret Russian lab in the American desert conducting psychic experiments during the Cold War thematically echoes the film's opening at Hangar 51 and the psychic powers of Irina Spalko."},{"source":"work_aw15","target":"work_aw321","type":"work_work","relation_type":"influenced","relation_note":"The character Eleven, a child with powerful psychokinetic abilities who escapes a secret government lab, strongly echoes the psychic espers (especially Akira himself) from the film."}],"stats":{"total_nodes":12,"total_edges":11,"hop_0_count":1,"hop_1_count":11,"hop_2_count":0,"hop_3_count":0,"phantom_count":12,"vault_count":0}}